{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_88a0fb686a124923b97b8e251838b059","id":"pg_9c08ac866c26595bbb094aebc42a01cc","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/cuga-project-cuga-agent-docs-issues-langfuse-nested-callback-propagati-4aebc42a01cc.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_69fdbf5ba0455e89bba75673aad3cef6"],"title":"cuga-project/cuga-agent/docs/issues/langfuse-nested-callback-propagation.md @ 65bdf2fb376d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_88a0fb686a124923b97b8e251838b059"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_3143a24bf47827b11ebaef5c10415e984df06a6786fe9250b1aaf5ee07e3ef75"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The provider exposes an A2A surface: a JSON-RPC endpoint at /a2a and an AgentCard at /.well-known/agent.json, per the example's documented URLs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_387132402162083678b17ab5dfc856bd77ecd06fd5b861bbc9f7539349432432"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A consumer supervisor config declares an external agent with a2a_protocol.transport=http; CUGA fetches the provider's AgentCard at startup, surfaces it as a tool, and delegates via delegate_task_via_a2a_sdk as JSON-RPC."},{"claim_ids":["clm_834c5449ca673302c888da5ed60bd4150578ef77b440b160d1f53f9d9c1f4d89"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A registry component serves the digital_sales OpenAPI tool catalog on http://localhost:8001, started with 'cuga start registry' in the example."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ae66b098d51a65b6acaedc17838de1120965c3910ae0b55a9e365fd5335cf33b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"In the A2A example both CUGAs run with auth_required=false, and the auth-token forwarding integration test is marked xfail until v1."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d5c6ed66aec551da1a1b2b4ea80dba83a4be9f8321f7ef27a0f8f6f106cf2b57"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The provider side uses a supervisor YAML declaring one internal agent (digital_sales) that pulls tools from the registry; DYNACONF_A2A__ENABLED=true and a supervisor config path env var route inbound A2A requests through it."}],"claim_ids":["clm_3143a24bf47827b11ebaef5c10415e984df06a6786fe9250b1aaf5ee07e3ef75","clm_387132402162083678b17ab5dfc856bd77ecd06fd5b861bbc9f7539349432432","clm_834c5449ca673302c888da5ed60bd4150578ef77b440b160d1f53f9d9c1f4d89","clm_ae66b098d51a65b6acaedc17838de1120965c3910ae0b55a9e365fd5335cf33b","clm_d5c6ed66aec551da1a1b2b4ea80dba83a4be9f8321f7ef27a0f8f6f106cf2b57"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_88a0fb686a124923b97b8e251838b059","id":"pg_9df204eec6b05bfbb66c5805df312fee","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/cuga-project-cuga-agent-docs-examples-a2a-two-cuga-readme-md-65bdf2fb3-5805df312fee.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_5f515d7fbb135d969f75cacb71e7f0dd"],"title":"cuga-project/cuga-agent/docs/examples/a2a_two_cuga/README.md @ 65bdf2fb376d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:55:58Z","updated_by_operation":"op_e618257034d04ab99a50460d223a8d62"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_88a0fb686a124923b97b8e251838b059","id":"pg_af78be658b425370b9480ecd5683dc24","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/cuga-project-cuga-agent-todos-md-65bdf2fb376d-0ecd5683dc24.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_8f96a160c9e3501cb9cc69d33b1c08b5"],"title":"cuga-project/cuga-agent/todos.md @ 65bdf2fb376d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_88a0fb686a124923b97b8e251838b059"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_02367a87d2e4f4f8b05da1cbb3dabfdcf9736ddf92d5d645602e66a2af37c40a"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A built-in knowledge engine ingests PDFs, Office files, HTML, Markdown, and images via Docling, with documents scoped either agent-level (permanent, shared) or session-level (per-thread, isolated)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_1933f7b06f479954cf4e927e175d9d24c20a1e3559135d64be36c83ab5b71e38"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration resolution priority is documented as environment variables highest, TOML configuration medium, and default values lowest."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2dcca38688ee0625eab95ed44b9ed9193fc99e8598ea5ec0d570a4ca0f9a2aec"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The final answer appears to be composed by a separately configurable LLM step that can be disabled in fast mode and shaped by a deterministic (str)->str function pointed at trusted code."},{"claim_ids":["clm_44ecd83571c6a22f7d89b48e6e9ff9ceda1d8216fe6dbd4da09e47a80acb2169"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Python SDK exposes CugaAgent(tools=[...]) with await agent.invoke(message), real-time agent.stream(), per-user thread_id session isolation, and access to the underlying LangGraph graph."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6a3dcfe435be68dfe795142ab616268cb78e4c87b9c1a9dd96357fa7855fadcd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The optional run receipt (run_receipt, default false) records tool data in timings-only mode: name, app, and duration only, never arguments, results, or errors, unless track_tool_calls=True is set."},{"claim_ids":["clm_806b4d140395e05f2309adbc0152cd9e79f7f65d9d09b1ba0499ee427f88786f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A single skills root is configured via [skills] root in settings.toml or DYNACONF_SKILLS__ROOT (default 'cuga'); CUGA scans one directory only, with no merge across paths."},{"claim_ids":["clm_88be92335b0883c5d5ad2646d943896646fa529af360bcf0e3ccdd8102b48187"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Skills are SKILL.md files with YAML frontmatter requiring name and description; CUGA lists short descriptions in the prompt and exposes a load_skill tool that returns the full markdown body on demand."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9e245e5659bbe63b23023cc50a9638cada6778118bc72cbe36ecb10809cff9c3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README claims #1 rankings on AppWorld (07/25–02/26, 750 tasks across 457 APIs) and WebArena (02/25–09/25); these are self-reported leaderboard positions, not measured in this snapshot."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c034bbe750f478f3d047b29b135dce470854222ee16ea19a1d8e36add1daf7d6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Documented LLM provider support includes OpenAI (plus LiteLLM via base URL override), IBM WatsonX, Azure OpenAI, Groq, RITS, OpenRouter, and watsonx Orchestrate, each with a dedicated settings TOML."}],"claim_ids":["clm_02367a87d2e4f4f8b05da1cbb3dabfdcf9736ddf92d5d645602e66a2af37c40a","clm_1933f7b06f479954cf4e927e175d9d24c20a1e3559135d64be36c83ab5b71e38","clm_2dcca38688ee0625eab95ed44b9ed9193fc99e8598ea5ec0d570a4ca0f9a2aec","clm_44ecd83571c6a22f7d89b48e6e9ff9ceda1d8216fe6dbd4da09e47a80acb2169","clm_6a3dcfe435be68dfe795142ab616268cb78e4c87b9c1a9dd96357fa7855fadcd","clm_806b4d140395e05f2309adbc0152cd9e79f7f65d9d09b1ba0499ee427f88786f","clm_88be92335b0883c5d5ad2646d943896646fa529af360bcf0e3ccdd8102b48187","clm_9e245e5659bbe63b23023cc50a9638cada6778118bc72cbe36ecb10809cff9c3","clm_c034bbe750f478f3d047b29b135dce470854222ee16ea19a1d8e36add1daf7d6"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:13Z","created_by_operation":"op_88a0fb686a124923b97b8e251838b059","id":"pg_d51ac25df3975dcd875daff10cb2d6ab","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/cuga-project-cuga-agent-readme-md-65bdf2fb376d-aff10cb2d6ab.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_265bdda968b45ba98ac228729504cd35"],"title":"cuga-project/cuga-agent/README.md @ 65bdf2fb376d","updated_at":"2026-09-14T01:44:13Z","updated_by_operation":"op_88a0fb686a124923b97b8e251838b059"}
